# Claude AI local files
.claude/

# Commit the repo-owned local-review skills while keeping other local Claude
# state ignored. Each level has to be re-opened explicitly: git will not descend
# into an excluded directory, so a leaf negation alone would never be consulted.
!.claude/
.claude/*
!.claude/skills/
.claude/skills/*
# Re-include only markdown, never `**`. Git applies patterns in file order and
# last match wins, so a recursive `!dir/**` here would sit *after* the *.key,
# *.pem, .env, *.p12 and *.pfx rules above and silently beat all of them,
# re-including any credential dropped into a skill directory. An allowlist cannot
# do that, and — unlike re-asserting the secret patterns by hand — it cannot go
# stale when a new one is added above. These brains are prose; if a skill ever
# needs a non-markdown file, add that extension here deliberately.
!.claude/skills/meeting-service-code-reviewer/
!.claude/skills/meeting-service-code-reviewer/**/
!.claude/skills/meeting-service-code-reviewer/**/*.md
!.claude/skills/meeting-service-learnings-reviewer/
!.claude/skills/meeting-service-learnings-reviewer/**/
!.claude/skills/meeting-service-learnings-reviewer/**/*.md
!.claude/skills/local-code-review
!.claude/skills/local-learnings-review
